ademy-id "q-18657" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨-2,0,1⟩$, $b=⟨5,2,-4⟩$ and $c=⟨1,0,3⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c).$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|-0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2(2\\cdot 3-(-4)\\cdot 0)-0+(5\\cdot 0-2\\cdot 1) \\\\  & =-12-0-2 \\\\  & =-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-18657/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff317cd2-0896-5134-b3a3-4e9f84e22b68"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-18657"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-20058"] :question/problem "Find $b\\cdot (c\\times a)$, if $-a\\cdot (3b\\times (-2c))=24.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor out the constants and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-a\\cdot (3b\\times (-2c)) & =24 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot 3\\cdot (-2)\\cdot [a\\cdot (b\\times c)] & =24 \\\\ a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $b$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\cdot (a\\times c) & =-4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand again we swap $a$ and $c$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\cdot (c\\times a) & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-73461/selection/ac46572169135c39bc2dc1bfb75349ed12f60a1187a3ef59cacec084b49d12ff" :answer/id #uuid "97944679-dcd7-5028-901c-7394f82b1f2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-23" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73461/selection/abe476e447976564bc5c670fe73789666287b967d49bbed12b1d85144449e63e" :answer/id #uuid "17db9901-26aa-50c9-a1e7-fcd35135796c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "23" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73461/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "329b48ae-1b91-5f67-b48d-81b66a8f8251" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73461/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "423f504d-0758-59f1-ad52-82baf54fd012" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73461/selection/23c0b4da815e7ba954fedc5e75955047cfe471feec4d2029849a63511c000fa3" :answer/id #uuid "7c9f7e62-cf90-54ea-8ab1-bfe3c6653003" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73461/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "79f78a99-f8c8-533d-8b12-55005d72a784" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73461/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-73461/selection/ac46572169135c39bc2dc1bfb75349ed12f60a1187a3ef59cacec084b49d12ff" "q-73461/selection/abe476e447976564bc5c670fe73789666287b967d49bbed12b1d85144449e63e" "q-73461/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-73461/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-73461/selection/23c0b4da815e7ba954fedc5e75955047cfe471feec4d2029849a63511c000fa3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73461" :question/id #uuid "03a4c208-a34c-5a3e-b51f-f4be25787fd5" :question/math-academy-id "q-73461" :question/problem "Let $p=⟨3,-2,1⟩$, $q=⟨2,-1,0⟩$ and $r=⟨1,-2,4⟩.$ Find $q\\cdot (r\\times p).$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the scalar triple product $q\\cdot (r\\times p)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $q,$ $r,$ and $p.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q\\cdot (r\\times p) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2((-2)\\cdot 1-4\\cdot (-2))+(1\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =12-11 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-73461/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff317cd2-0896-5134-b3a3-4e9f84e22b68"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73461"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-317325/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "8c5ecfdb-e402-5398-a023-358139ea8488" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-317325/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9632f951-4e44-5089-ae7f-a3d6c4779422" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-317325/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-317325/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-317325" :question/id #uuid "c0fb786c-c205-5d9a-a424-74286effcd4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-317325" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨-1,-2,3⟩$, $b=⟨4,-1,-2⟩$ and $c=⟨1,2,-3⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using a determinant.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}|\\,-\\,(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|\\,+\\,3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\,((-1)(-3)-(-2)\\cdot 2)\\,-\\,(-2)\\,(4\\cdot (-3)-(-2)\\cdot 1)\\,+\\,3\\,(4\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 1) \\\\  & =(-1)\\,(7)\\,-\\,(-2)\\,(-10)\\,+\\,3\\,(9) \\\\  & =-7-20+27 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-317325/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff317cd2-0896-5134-b3a3-4e9f84e22b68"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-317325"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
